---
name: line-world-hyperframes
description: Synchronizes and renders Line World video compositions with one seekable clock, continuous camera motion, linked specialist assets and editable timing. Use inside the video plugin for clean full-frame D3/Mermaid/Iconify films and final MP4 verification.
---

# Line World HyperFrames

Read the [video contract](references/video-contract.md). Own the film clock,
assembly, camera and export, while specialist copies own their actual assets.

1. Define one project-owned story with dimensions, fps, data status, units,
   scene partitions, durations, focus IDs and palette reason. Allocate complete
   frame sections and reading holds before animating.
2. Compose real D3 groups, native Mermaid SVG and licensed icons. Keep a stable
   identity map and data model across representations. Namespace imported SVG
   IDs, styles, markers and ARIA targets. Keep the wider world persistent.
3. Default to a clean white stage with thin geometry. Do not add title cards,
   captions, headers, chapter badges, closing slogans, promotional transitions,
   stock decoration or audio merely because a video renderer supports them.
   Add requested contextual words only to the specified scene.
4. Expose pure `window.renderAt(seconds)` and an inspectable state snapshot.
   Register a paused HyperFrames/GSAP timeline which drives this one clock.
   Do not run independent producer timers. Separate arrival, reveal, dot travel
   and reading holds. Use restrained pans and scales rather than camera shake.
5. Keep preview play, scrub, speed, section selection and drag controls outside
   the composition. Put exported durations in editable story data and derive
   all boundaries and highlights from it. Preview speed is not export timing.
6. Run actual native lint/runtime/layout checks, render the MP4, decode it and
   verify dimensions, fps, duration, frame count, legibility and final state.
   Keep native and browser-fallback evidence distinct. Use local HTML and
   deterministic browser capture when the native renderer is unavailable.
7. Deliver the movie, editable project, timing/coverage manifests and actual
   validation results. Use no automatically added closing title.

The copied [producer workflows](references/producer-workflows.md) provide
mechanism modeling, asset import and engine operations when needed. Their
primitive scaffold is a synchronization fallback, not a reason to add UI or
generic boxes. The video contract sets this plugin copy's default aesthetics.
